{"id": 36, "ts": 1780414042.3821409, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate that Sarah and James have both backed Candidate\u202fC, largely because of his ability to make correct decisions quickly\u2014a clear strength for decision quality. However, I\u2019m increasingly concerned that his difficulty communicating ideas, his egocentric reputation, and his lack of willingness to pursue further education raise serious red flags for crew cooperation, professional communication, and adaptability\u2014criteria that are non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011distance operations. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB demonstrates very strong operational reliability (very conscientious) and excellent stress resilience (handles stress very well), plus solid technical competence (good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills). While B can be perceived as pretentious and sometimes uses the wrong tone, those issues seem less likely to impair safety than C\u2019s communication deficits. Therefore, I\u2019m shifting my provisional recommendation to Candidate\u202fB, as his strengths align more comprehensively with the critical pilot criteria."}
